# stack-drift — let the unprivileged drift monitor verify the root-only policy
# files it tracks, and nothing else.
#
# Scope is deliberately as small as it can be while still being useful:
#   * read-only. `cat`, never an editor, never a shell.
#   * exact paths as literal arguments. No wildcards, so this cannot be turned into
#     a read primitive for any other root-owned file.
#   * both files' contents already live in the pi5-stack repo and in
#     ~/ap-testbed/sudoers.d-ap-testbed, so this discloses nothing the operator
#     account cannot already read. The grant buys verification, not access.
#   * /etc/sudoers.d is 0755 root:root and its files are 0440 root:root, so the
#     unprivileged user cannot swap either path for a symlink to something else.
#
# Without this the daily job can only report /etc/sudoers.d/ap-testbed as
# "unreadable, not checked" — a permanent blind spot in the one file that defines
# what the portal is allowed to do as root.
__STACK_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/cat /etc/sudoers.d/ap-testbed, /usr/bin/cat /etc/sudoers.d/stack-drift
